SUMMARY:Berchtoldstag
DESCRIPTION:History: Medieval Swiss guilds observed Berchtoldstag as a post
 -feast day to honor community bonds and start the civic year together.\nTra
 ditions: Families make Berchteln visits\, children knock on doors during Ba
 erzelistag parades\, and neighbors share well wishes with carved masks or p
ine boughs.\nFeasting: Tables feature braided Zopf loaves\, roesti skillets
\, sausages\, hazelnut tortes\, and pots of melted cheese for communal dipp
 ing.\nDay: Friday\n\nIcon: 🍞\nCategory: cultural
CATEGORIES:cultural
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
