SUMMARY:Fete de Papa Zaka - Feast of the Farmer Loa
DESCRIPTION:History: Haitian Vodou communities honour Papa Zaka, the kindly fa
 rmer lwa, during January gatherings to thank him for guarding crops and labou
 ring families.\nTraditions: Altars are dressed with straw hats, ears of corn,
  bowls of grain, rum, and pipe tobacco while drummers, singers, and vodouisan
 ts petition Zaka for fertile fields before sharing food with neighbours.\nFea
 sting: Aperitifs pour clairin ti punch, kleren anisette, and pumpkin-spice ju
 s giraumon; first courses carry soup joumou, accra de morue with pikliz, and 
 mayi moulen ak sos pwa; mains feature poulet nan sos, griot de porc, legim na
 n diri, and red beans with rice; sides bring bannann peze, pain mayi, and jar
 s of pikliz; desserts finish with pen patat, bonbons sirop, tropical fruits, 
 and altar offerings of roasted corn, a grain-filled straw hat, and a shot of 
 rum with pipe tobacco.\nDay: Saturday\n\nIcon: 🌾\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCategory: cul
 tural\\\\\\
CATEGORIES:cultural\\\\\\
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
