SUMMARY:Fete du Vodoun (Benin Vodoun Festival)
DESCRIPTION:History: Benin recognised Vodoun as a national religion in 1996
 \, formalising annual January gatherings that honour ancestral spirits and 
 the transatlantic heritage of resistance.\nTraditions: Processions of pries
 ts\, devotees\, and Egungun dancers drum along Ouidah's Route des Esclaves\
 , offering libations at the Temple of Pythons and the seaside.\nFeasting: F
 estival goers share akassa corn porridge\, goat and fish stews flavoured wi
 th palm oil\, toasted peanuts\, and generous pours of sodabi palm liquor.\n
 Day: Saturday\n\nIcon: 🎭\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCategory: cultural\\\\\\
CATEGORIES:cultural\\\\\\
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-IMAGE:https://dcmcshan.github.io/MaybeSomethingSeasonal/images/vodoun-festival-traditional-celebration-in-benin-honoring-vodoun-spirituality-an.png
END:VEVENT
