SUMMARY:Burns Night Supper
DESCRIPTION:History: The first Burns Night was held in 1801 by friends of R
 obert Burns\, celebrating the Bard's January birth with readings that cemen
 ted his role in Scottish identity.\nTraditions: Kilted hosts pipe in the ha
 ggis\, deliver the Address with flourish\, toast the lassies\, and end with
  ceilidh dances and "Auld Lang Syne."\nFeasting: Menus centre on haggis wit
 h neeps and tatties\, cock-a-leekie soup\, cranachan\, oatcakes\, and drams
  of smoky single malt whisky.\nDay: Sunday\n\nIcon: 🏴󠁧󠁢󠁳󠁣󠁴󠁿\\\\\\\\\
 \\\\\\nCategory: cultural\\\\\\
CATEGORIES:cultural\\\\\\
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
