SUMMARY:Lunar New Year (Chunjie)
DESCRIPTION:History: Rooted in Han dynasty agrarian cycles\, the Lunar New 
 Year welcomes spring with family reunions\, ancestor veneration\, and hopes
  for prosperity.\nTraditions: Homes are scrubbed\, red lanterns strung\, ho
 ngbao envelopes gifted\, and lion or dragon dances chase away lingering Nia
 n monsters.\nFeasting: Reunion banquets showcase longevity noodles\, whole 
 fish\, dumplings shaped like ingots\, sweet rice cakes\, and mandarin orang
 es for abundance.\nDay: Thursday\n\nIcon: 🐉\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCategory: cultu
 ral\\\\\\
CATEGORIES:cultural\\\\\\
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-IMAGE:https://dcmcshan.github.io/MaybeSomethingSeasonal/images/lunar-new-year-celebration.png
