SUMMARY:Imbolc Eve (La Fheile Bride)
DESCRIPTION:History: Imbolc heralds the first stirrings of spring in ancien
 t Gaelic tradition\, bridged later with the veneration of Saint Brigid of K
 ildare.\nTraditions: Families fashion Brigid's crosses\, set out corn dolli
 es to receive the saint's blessing\, and keep vigil fires burning through t
 he night.\nFeasting: Dairy-rich dishes--fresh butter\, soft cheeses\, oatca
 kes\, and early lamb stews--honour Brigid's patronage of livestock and the 
 hearth.\nDay: Friday\n\nIcon: 🌙\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCategory: seasonal\\\\\\
CATEGORIES:seasonal\\\\\\
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-IMAGE:https://dcmcshan.github.io/MaybeSomethingSeasonal/images/eve-of-imbolc-the-celtic-festival-marking-the-beginning-of-spring.png
