SUMMARY:All Hallows' Eve (Halloween)
DESCRIPTION:History: Halloween evolved from Celtic Samhain festivals and me
 dieval vigils before All Saints' Day\, blending remembrance with merrymakin
 g.\nTraditions: Costumed revelers carve jack-o'-lanterns\, tell ghost stori
 es\, visit haunted houses\, and children collect sweets door to door.\nFeas
 ting: Seasonal treats include candy apples\, pumpkin bread\, roasted nuts\,
  soul cakes\, and steaming mugs of spiced cider.\nDay: Saturday\n\nIcon: 🎃
