SUMMARY:Dia de los Muertos
DESCRIPTION:History: Rooted in pre-Hispanic customs later intertwined with 
 Catholic All Souls' rites\, Dia de los Muertos celebrates ancestral continu
 ity on 2 November.\nTraditions: Families build ofrendas with photos and cop
 al incense\, picnic beside candlelit graves\, and share stories through the
  night.\nFeasting: Traditional dishes include pan de muerto\, mole\, tamale
 s\, champurrado\, and calaveras de azucar painted with loved ones' names.\n
 Day: Sunday\n\nIcon: 💀\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCategory: cultural\\\\\\
