SUMMARY:Martinstag Lantern Evening
DESCRIPTION:History: Eves of St. Martin's Day in German-speaking lands reca
 ll the charitable Roman soldier turned bishop who shared his cloak with a b
 eggar.\nTraditions: Children carry handmade lanterns through the streets\, 
 sing Sankt Martin songs\, and end with bonfires or shadow plays retelling h
 is compassion.\nFeasting: Warm cider\, pretzels\, roasted chestnuts\, and b
 uttery pastries reward lantern bearers after the chilly evening walk.\nDay:
  Monday\n\nIcon: 🪶\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCategory: cultural\\\\\\
